-- title:
--   U_q²=1 in the localised Hecke algebra at a Steinberg prime
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for its maximal ideal and with finite residue field $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, let $p$ be a prime with $p \in \mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$: a two-dimensional $k$-vector space with a monoid homomorphism $\bar\rho.\rho$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ to its endomorphisms factoring through a finite level, assumed absolutely irreducible in the sense that its base change to $\overline k$ is irreducible. Let $S_0 \subseteq S$ be finite sets of natural numbers all of whose elements are prime, with $p \in S$, and let $N \neq 0$ be such that every prime divisor of $N$ lies in $S$ and none lies in $S_0$; it is assumed that the $\mathbb Z$-lattice of weight-two cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$ with integral $q$-expansion coefficients spans the whole space over $\mathbb C$. Let $\theta'$ be a ring homomorphism to $k$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S_0$, together with the $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$, $q \notin S_0$. Assume $\theta'$ matches $\bar\rho$ outside $S$: for every prime $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $P$, and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ and inducing $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho.\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - \theta'(T_\ell)X + \ell$. Finally let $q$ be a prime with $q \neq p$, $q \mid N$ and $q^2 \nmid N$, and suppose $\bar\rho$ is not unramified at $q$, i.e. some valuation subring over $q$ has an element of its inertia subgroup acting non-trivially. Then the image of $U_q$ under the structure map [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.π`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L151) into the localisation of $\mathcal O \otimes_{\mathbb Z}$ `heckeAlgebra N 2 S₀` at the prime cut out by $\theta'$ satisfies $U_q^2 = 1$.
--
--   This is the Steinberg-prime relation $U_q^2 = 1$ in the Hecke algebra localised at a residual eigensystem, for a prime $q$ exactly dividing the level at which the residual representation is ramified; classically it reflects the fact that such an eigenform is a twist of a form with $U_q$-eigenvalue $\pm 1$. It feeds the corner/level-structure analysis at a Steinberg prime, being cited by [`CohCarrier.exists_sq_eq_one_and_heckeT_eq_smul_of_mem_cornerSubmodule_of_not_isUnramifiedAt_of_ringHom`](thm.html#CohCarrier.exists_sq_eq_one_and_heckeT_eq_smul_of_mem_cornerSubmodule_of_not_isUnramifiedAt_of_ringHom).
